From 2ec9ec7189705aaeb291fee7b8b80f084d9936cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:31:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: calibrate the EN7580 RX equalizer from eye
 data

The recovered EN7580 startup tables omit XFI_EO_Scan(), which the XGZ030
GPL executes between RX L2D transition and RX ready. The missing scan
leaves receive equalization at its fixed preset even when another
peaking value yields a larger eye opening.

Port the normal eight-point LEQ peaking scan with gain fixed at 1, using
the mode-specific setup, calibration strobes and measurement delays
from en7580_xsi_pma.i. Split the existing start table before RX ready so
all original operations retain their order around the new calibration.

Only accept completed horizontal and vertical measurements. Preserve the
first best setting on ties and restore the original gain and peaking if
no completed measurement has a positive opening, including boot without
a signal. Reproduce the vendor CDR tracking restart when HEO is not ready.
Sleep during long measurement windows and propagate register access
errors while the MAC gates and PCS reset remain held.

The source is sdk/en7580/linux-4.4.115/en7580_xsi_pma.i in the
XGZ030 v1 GPL.

Validation: MIPS32 little-endian PCS object build, checkpatch, original
sequence preservation, and native register-backend comparisons against
the GPL C for all four modes with ties, incomplete/no-signal/zero-eye
fallback and 1524 register-access fault cases. Hardware testing pending.
